\ A helper defined inside an `if` arm and read there. The arm was captured when it was pushed, and
\ the interpreter answers a read inside it from that capture before the arm's own definition. So
\ the read is not compiled to the helper's body, and the build refuses the word.

arm-helper: ( n: fixnum -- n ) [
  dup 0 > [ bump: [ 1 + ] ; bump ] [ ] if
] ;

3 arm-helper .
